        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1460f501-12dc-5ba5-899d-c53d29ed05e6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eric Liddell, Harold Abrahams, Evelyn Aubrey Montague\n- Organizations: Achilles Club\n- Products: Chariots of Fire\n- Events: 1924 Olympics\n- Concepts: Christianity, Judaism, prejudice, missionary work\n\nFacts:\n- Eric Henry Liddell was born on 16 January 1902 and later became a Scottish athlete, a rugby union international player, and a missionary.\n- Chariots of Fire tells a fact-based story about two athletes at the 1924 Olympics: Eric Liddell, a devout Scottish Christian, and Harold Abrahams, an English Jew.\n- In Chariots of Fire, Eric Liddell runs for the glory of God, while Harold Abrahams runs to overcome prejudice.\n- Eric Liddell chose his religious beliefs over competing in an Olympic race that was held on a Sunday.\n- Evelyn Aubrey Montague was one of the founding members of the Achilles Club.\n- Evelyn Aubrey Montague was immortalized in the 1981 film Chariots of Fire.\n- Eric Henry Liddell died on 21 February 1945.",
